# PART 3 — CORE GAME DESIGN PHILOSOPHY

These principles must influence every important design decision.

## 3.1 Accessibility without sacrificing depth

The game must be immediately understandable to players who have little or no railway knowledge.

Players should be able to understand:

- Where each train is travelling.
- Which track it intends to use.
- Why it is waiting.
- Which signal is controlling its movement.
- What is preventing it from proceeding.
- What action can resolve the situation.

Complexity should emerge gradually through gameplay rather than being dumped on the player through an enormous tutorial.

## 3.2 Meaningful decisions

Do not make gameplay consist exclusively of repeatedly tapping switches.

Players should have to consider:

- Which train deserves priority.
- Whether a platform will be available.
- Whether a junction should be reserved.
- Whether a freight train should wait.
- Whether an alternative route is available.
- Whether two trains may create a conflict.
- Whether maintaining a timetable is worth delaying another service.

Every decision should have understandable consequences.

## 3.3 Immediate satisfaction

Players should experience frequent positive feedback.

Examples:

- A successful junction clearance.
- A train arriving at its destination.
- A complicated route conflict being resolved.
- Several trains operating without delays.
- A series of consecutive successful deliveries.
- A perfectly coordinated platform assignment.

Casual modes should provide satisfying experiences within minutes.

## 3.4 Fair difficulty

Difficulty must arise from interacting railway systems.

Do not make the game difficult through unfair random events, impossible traffic configurations or arbitrary reaction-time requirements.

A difficult situation must remain understandable and potentially solvable.

## 3.5 Long-term replayability

The game must not become exhausted after completing a short campaign.

Provide multiple forms of replayability:

- Structured campaign content.
- Short self-contained challenges.
- Timed casual operations.
- Endless high-score gameplay.
- Relaxed free play.
- Player-created railway networks.

Do not rely on artificial grinding to create playtime.

