# PART 19 — AUTOMATED TESTING

Create tests for the underlying railway simulation.

At minimum, verify:

1. A train follows a valid route.
2. Invalid routes are rejected.
3. A red signal prevents entry.
4. Conflicting sections cannot be occupied simultaneously.
5. Conflicting routes cannot be reserved simultaneously.
6. Switches respect occupancy and reservations.
7. Long trains occupy the appropriate track sections.
8. Carriages follow trains through curves.
9. Trains respect braking distance.
10. Platforms cannot host incompatible simultaneous movements.
11. Pausing correctly stops simulation progression.
12. Simulation speed changes do not corrupt the simulation.
13. Deadlock conditions are detected.
14. Invalid railway configurations are rejected.
15. Saved layouts can be restored.
16. Campaign progress survives application restart.
17. Rush Hour sessions produce valid train schedules.
18. Endless Flow generation produces solvable configurations.
19. Quick Dispatch challenges are playable to completion.
20. Casual records persist correctly.

Also perform manual gameplay testing.

A successful compilation does not prove that the game is fun or that train routing is correct.

Do not claim tests passed unless they have actually been executed.

